    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it doesn't feel like \"protection\" though. it feels more like i've just seen too much of how hollow everything actually is. everything people care about—the jobs, the small talk, the pointless errands—it all feels so fake. it’s like i'm operating on a completely different frequency than they are. it's exhausting trying to pretend i'm part of it.",
